menu "WiFi Dap proxy (USBIP / WebSocket-DAP)"

    config BIRDIEBOT_DAP_WS_ENABLE
        bool "Enable the legacy WebSocket-DAP transport (TCP 3240)"
        default y
        help
            Accepts a WebSocket-DAP session on the DAP proxy port
            (components/dap_proxy/websocket_server.c): the client upgrades
            from HTTP with "GET ", then sends binary frames whose payload is a
            CMSIS-DAP command packet.

            This is an unauthenticated, plain-text transport: enable it only
            on a trusted LAN (docs/INTEGRATION-PLAN.md P7.1).  Disable it to
            run USBIP and elaphureLink only; the port stays open for those
            two protocols.

            Default: y (laboratory mode, same as the fork).

    config BIRDIEBOT_USBIP_PIPELINE
        bool "Enable multi-URB USBIP pipeline (B1)"
        default y
        help
            Decouples the USBIP TCP reader from the DAP command execution so
            that several URBs can be in flight per Wi-Fi round-trip (the host
            kernel vhci + OpenOCD cmsis-dap keep up to 3 pending requests).
            OUT URBs are ACKed immediately and IN URBs are answered by the DAP
            task when the matching response is ready; UNLINKs keep the
            response/IN FIFOs aligned.  The legacy single-URB path is used when
            this option is disabled or the pipeline detects an inconsistency.

            Default: y (same transport, lower latency on a real Wi-Fi link).

    config BIRDIEBOT_USBIP_TCP_CORE
        int "Core affinity of the USBIP tcp_server task"
        range 0 1
        default 1
        help
            The DAP task must run on core 1 (dedicated-GPIO SWD bit-banging).
            Keeping the USBIP tcp_server task on core 1 (default) minimizes the
            hand-off latency to the DAP task; core 0 decouples the Wi-Fi/lwIP
            handling from the DAP bit-banging CPU time.  Both placements are
            measured in the B1 hardware window.

    config BIRDIEBOT_USBIP_TCP_PRIORITY
        int "Priority of the USBIP tcp_server task"
        range 5 24
        default 14
        help
            FreeRTOS priority of the USBIP/EL/WS-DAP TCP task.  The DAP command
            task priority is BIRDIEBOT_DAP_TASK_PRIORITY (default 16); raising
            this above the DAP task lets network ACKs preempt SWD bit-banging,
            lowering the per-URB latency at some SWD throughput cost.

    config BIRDIEBOT_DAP_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Priority of the DAP command task"
        range 5 24
        default 16

    config BIRDIEBOT_DAP_PACKET_SIZE
        int "DAP packet size reported to the debugger (bytes, ESP32-S3)"
        range 256 4048
        default 1280
        help
            CMSIS-DAP packet size returned by DAP_Info and used for the USBIP
            stage2 payload buffer.  The USBIP transport is latency-bound, so a
            larger packet means more SWD data per OUT+IN URB round-trip.

            OpenOCD 0.12 (cmsis-dap DAP_Transfer, u8 transfer count) derives its
            block size as (packet-4)/5 and is only correct up to 1280
            ((1280-4)/5 = 255 transfers).  OpenOCD master uses DAP_TransferBlock
            (u16 count) and can use a much larger packet (e.g. 4000-4048);
            this is A/B measured in the B1 hardware window and the release
            default is chosen from that data.

            Other targets are fixed at 1024 by main/dap_configuration.h.

endmenu
